//==
// # Meshed witnesses (complexity sweep, chunk L1)
//
// A model meshed once per sweep under the witness options, so a law over it reads the mesh and
// the report instead of calling MeshModel per case (testing strategy, part a; TKT-356). The law
// runner builds every Witness_* of these types once, before any law runs, and exhausts the finite
// list for a law parameter of the type: neither type is generatable, since both hold a ModelMesh
// or a PipelineState.

// A model and the outcome of meshing it with MeshModel under the witness options.
// Invariant: Outcome is Model.MeshModel(MeshingOptions.WitnessOptions).
type MeshedWitness
{
    Name: String;
    Model: BrepModel;
    Outcome: MeshOutcome;
}

// A meshed model with one face the mesher refuses, and the three loop states the
// failure-isolation laws read: the first state and the final state of the run over every face,
// and the final state of the run with Face left out. Kept apart from MeshedWitness so the laws over
// every MeshedWitness state what a positive witness meshes to, with no exception for this one.
// Invariant: Meshed's outcome is the run Final ends; all three states use the witness options.
type FailedFaceWitness
{
    Meshed: MeshedWitness;
    Face: BrepFaceIndex;
    Initial: PipelineState;
    Final: PipelineState;
    Dropped: PipelineState;
}
